PHASE 3 — SIMPLIFY EACH CLOSED PROJECT CARD
==================================================

The current cards contain too many repeated ways to open the same project.

We do not need:

- A small arrow at the top.
- Another arrow at the bottom.
- A View Project button.
- An additional Step Inside button.
- Another input-like action performing the same task.

Simplify the OUTER BlueMind card.

Use no more than TWO visible opening affordances:

1. One main “View Demo” CTA.
2. One optional, clearly recognizable expand icon in the top-right.

The card’s preview area can trigger the same opening action.
Do not add another button simply to make the whole card clickable.

Use ONE consistent CTA label across all cards:

View Demo

Keep:

- The project cover.
- The project name.
- Its concept category.
- One short description.

Remove redundant opening controls from the outer presentation.

IMPORTANT DISTINCTION:

The demo website itself may legitimately contain buttons such as:
Add to Bag, Generate, View Menu, Reserve a Table, etc.

Do NOT remove those internal project buttons.

Only remove duplicate BlueMind-level controls around the project card.

If a closed card uses a miniature rendered website as its cover, that miniature should not expose competing clickable controls. It is a preview until the full demo is opened.

Avoid nested buttons or a link containing other interactive controls.

