Keep icon sizing and stroke weight consistent.

Hover should be simple:

- Slight tonal change.
- Clear pointer feedback.
- No layout shift.
- No dramatic circle enlargement.
- No floating decorative marks.

Do not rely on color alone to explain the action.
Provide accessible names and clear focus styles.

==================================================
PHASE 6 — MAKE ALL THREE CONTROLS FUNCTIONAL
==================================================

RED — CLOSE

Close the project viewer using the same smooth exit animation as the regular close/back action.

After closing:

- Restore the BlueMind page’s previous scroll position.
- Restore keyboard focus to the card/control that opened the project.
- Release background scroll locking.
- Leave no invisible overlay blocking the page.

YELLOW — MINIMIZE

Minimize the currently opened project to a compact restore control.

This is not the same action as closing.

Preserve the current demo state, including relevant local interactions such as:

- Cart contents.
- Selected filters.
- AI demo result.
- Form draft.
- Internal scroll position.

Show one compact control containing:

Project name
Restore

The visitor should be able to restore the same project without starting over.

Do not keep hidden demo controls keyboard-focusable while minimized.

The compact restore control must not cover important page buttons or create horizontal overflow.

Support one active/minimized project at a time.
Do not build a desktop-style multi-window management system.

GREEN — EXPAND / RESTORE

Toggle between:

Normal viewer size
Expanded viewer size

Expanded means using the available browser area more fully.

Keep the toolbar and exit controls visible.

Clicking again restores the previous viewer size.

Prefer in-page expansion.
Do not request browser-native fullscreen or attempt to control the actual operating-system window.

IMPORTANT:

Expanding the viewer must not automatically switch the selected device mode.

For example:

If Mobile mode is selected, expanding the outer viewer must still display the mobile-layout preview.

All controls must have actual behavior.
Do not leave yellow and green as decorative fake buttons.

